THE NOISE IS NAMED RATHER THAN HIDDEN. Of the 119 sites raised against each
host_fs claim, 63 are `.replace()` -- overwhelmingly str.replace, the literal
INV-maluk collision, which the gate cannot match but can and now does
disclose. The remainder is not noise: mkdir 19, write_text 12, write 11,
unlink 9, rename/truncate/touch; the network claim raises write 11, close 6,
send_json 1. This is what _MAX_REPORTED_UNTYPED_SITES was for -- above five
sites the sentence names distinct METHODS instead of locations, so a reader
discounts `replace` and acts on `mkdir`.

SECURITY.md's "Known limitations" said receiver typing is incomplete and left
it unquantified. It now states the measured bound on hypergumbo's own tree:
6,541 of 9,267 method call sites (70.6%) have a receiver the analysis could
not type. That figure bounds every verdict in its table.

Gate green and stable across two independent runs (no nondeterminism in the
pinned caveat kinds). 4616 passed, 100% coverage, ratchet 670.

